    "public_summary": "Iran's internet remains in stable partial outage with one notable change: Irancell's international gateway shifted from silent packet drop to active TCP RST injection between passes, suggesting a DPI policy state change. All 4 major ISP gateways remain unreachable while domestic and whitelisted foreign services operate normally. The selective-internet architecture is stable at 4.1% reachability (44/1068). Saman Bank latency improved to 2,891ms, crossing below the 3-second threshold. Electro DNS suppression, Snapp redirect-loop, and Shaparak timeout all persist unchanged. All circumvention tools and foreign platforms remain fully accessible.",
    "insight": "The Irancell gateway's transition from silent drop (timeout) to active RST injection (connection refused) between consecutive passes is the only meaningful state change — this likely reflects DPI appliance failover or a new filtering rule deployment shifting the rejection mode from passive to active, a pattern consistent with periodic maintenance cycles within the stealth blackout architecture rather than a policy escalation.",
